      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**The work order and Pending Close time are confirmed, but the available records do not support a complete event-level conclusion.** The assigned supporting records returned “Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”\n\n| Review item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| September cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Unavailable |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event’s type, timing, and status |\n\nThe source timestamp does not specify a time zone, so I have preserved it exactly.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\nThe supplied Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B documentation, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 (printed page 225)**, states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are **not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Previously entered transactions continue processing. Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary, non-exempt transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held from processing. However, **I cannot establish whether such an event exists for this work order or judge its recorded status from the supplied evidence**. The missing cost-event records must be made available to finish the review.\n\nNo database records were changed. The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_34de18f3d13f/audit-report.json`.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
